# Qibla Compass Enhancement Plan

We need to upgrade the basic Qibla compass implementation to be highly accurate, use "Islamic premium design", and provide tactile feedback when aligned with Mecca.

## User Review Required

> [!WARNING]
> We will need to install `expo-haptics` to provide physical feedback when pointing towards Mecca. Is it okay to add this dependency?
> 
> Also, different devices (especially Android) sometimes have flaky Magnetometer readings. I plan to use `Location.watchHeadingAsync` to get a stable compass heading from the OS directly.

## Proposed Changes

### Core Dependencies

#### [NEW] Dependencies
- `expo-haptics` mapped to `npx expo install expo-haptics`
- `react-native-reanimated` mapped to `npx expo install react-native-reanimated` (for smooth dial rotations)

---

### UI and Components

#### [MODIFY] src/screens/QiblaScreen.tsx
- Replace the raw `Magnetometer` API reading with `Location.watchHeadingAsync` to ensure tilt-compensated compass accuracy.
- Create a beautiful rotating Compass UI using structured layered Views matching the currently established Emerald and Amber theme.
- Implement Haptic Feedback (`Haptics.impactAsync`) using `expo-haptics` when the user aligns their device perfectly (e.g. within 3 degrees of the Qibla).
- Add visual indicators (a glowing effect or clear amber text reading "Aligned") when you align with the Kaaba.

